Package: prime
Type: Package
Title: Proportional Inclusive Marginal Effects
Version: 0.5.2.9101
Authors@R: c(
    person("Youngseo", "Cho", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "ycho397@gatech.edu"),
    person("V. Roshan", "Joseph", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           email = "roshan@gatech.edu")
  )
Description: Estimates proportional global variable importance for noisy
    input-response data with dependent predictors. A response-relevant screen
    adapts 'FIRST' from Huang and Joseph (2025)
    <doi:10.1080/00401706.2025.2483531> using local-linear residualization,
    a Bayesian-information-criterion-gated ridge start, and query-calibrated
    forward and backward comparisons. Proportional allocation follows Herin et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1137/22M153032X>. Exact nearest-neighbor searches use the full
    sample by default; deterministic 'Data Twinning' from Vakayil and Joseph
    (2022) <doi:10.1002/sam.11574> can reduce the outer query average.
